# Miracles and extraordinary events — eyewitness and process testimony (M-EW)

Each entry is a report, not a finding. Sorted by the first year in its title or report; undated last. Status lines say whether the event was sworn at a process, listed in the vice-postulator's Articles (1910), or only reported. Approved miracles: beatification 1923 — Abbé Charles Anne, Sr Louise de Saint-Germain; canonization 1925 — Maria Pellemans, Sr Gabriella Trimusi (plan §8.1). Several entries describe the same event from different witnesses (e.g. Gallipoli, Aubry, Anne); they are kept apart.

### M-EW-001 — Zélie's inner voice: "Fais faire du Point d'Alençon" (Alençon, c. 1851–53)
- Period: Martin family, before Thérèse's birth
- What was reported: On the feast of the Immaculate Conception, making her bed, Zélie heard "Have Point d'Alençon made"; she started the business the next day.
- The person helped: Zélie Guérin (Martin)
- Witnesses and reporter: Zélie told Marie
- Status: family tradition
- Source: MSC, Cahier
- Medical or natural facts mentioned: none
- Doubts / other versions: Marie says Zélie ascribed it to the Virgin; told decades later.
- Extraction ID: J-M06

### M-EW-002 — Aunt Sr Marie-Dosithée recovers before Marie's First Communion (Le Mans, c. 1869)
- Period: Martin family
- What was reported: The aunt was gravely ill; Marie's First Communion was advanced a year so she could see it. Marie, at nine, threw jasmine crowns to St Joseph and was sure of a cure. The aunt recovered, attended, and lived seven more years; dying, she told Marie she owed her seven years of life.
- The person helped: Sr Marie-Dosithée Guérin
- Witnesses and reporter: Marie
- Status: family memory
- Source: MSC, Cahier
- Medical or natural facts mentioned: breathing distress ("oppressée"); all hope seemed lost weeks before
- Doubts / other versions: Marie says she lived seven years; she died 1877 — dates roughly consistent.
- Extraction ID: J-M08

