### M-EW-005 — The baby found on a chair (Thérèse, Alençon, 1874)
- Period: during life
- What was reported: Returning from early Mass, Zélie found the baby's place empty, then found the child asleep sitting on a high chair. Marie: she had fallen from her cradle and could not have climbed the chair herself; the mother saw God's intervention. Céline: Zélie had left her in the big bed and forgot to bring the cradle close to stop her falling; she found her on a chair and could not understand how.
